{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The three artifacts describe the same trip, so the rider's initial burden under POL-RD-08(a) is discharged: trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown all carry trip identifier TRP-02819 and the trace runs from the recorded trip-start at 16:25:31 to trip-completion at 16:32:51. The trace is also unimpaired for policy purposes - 100.0% coverage, 45 fixes at a 10-second sample interval, zero gaps and a maximum inter-fix gap of 0.0 seconds - so no consequence under POL-RD-07(a) to (c) arises and the distance it measures stands as the measured distance for this trip.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02819", "EV-GPS-02819", "EV-FARE-02819"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08", "POL-RD-07"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "On the governing trace figure of 3.96 km against the booked optimal of 3.2 km, the excess is 0.76 km, which is 23.75% of the optimal route and therefore above POL-RD-01's 20% percentage limb. POL-RD-01 requires this measurement to be taken from gps_trace.trace_distance_km, not from the rounded 4.0 km convenience copy on the trip record, and the rider cites the trace figure. I do not put the percentage limb forward as establishing the deviation on its own, because the clause requires both limbs to pass and the rider addresses the second limb squarely in a separate claim below.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02819", "EV-TRIP-02819"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_pct",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's only explanation on file is 'One-way streets'. That is an external traffic cause asserted with no evidence ID, and there is no traffic_advisory in this bundle: EV-ADVIS-02819-01 is MISSING, its weight_multiplier is 0.0 and the issue code that fired is MISSING_ARTIFACT (severity BLOCKING). Under POL-RD-13 the assertion is tested against the traffic_advisory for this trip and nothing else, so POL-RD-03 cannot be run on the record and the assertion carries no weight under POL-RD-08, which discards assertions that cite no evidence ID. I disclose the impairment of the artifact I rely on: EV-ADVIS-02819-01 is cited for its absence alone, which POL-GEN-02(3) makes citable. The driver's account also has no artifact behind it at all - the chat log for this trip carries zero messages from either party.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-02819-01", "EV-CHAT-02819", "EV-GPS-02819"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-13", "POL-RD-08", "POL-RD-03", "POL-GEN-02"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No clause on this record supplies the driver with an amended optimal or with any reduction of the measured excess. The chat log carries zero messages, so POL-RD-04's rider-instruction route is unavailable and its 200 m corroboration test cannot be run on the record; both pickup_amended_at and dropoff_amended_at are null and amended_optimal_distance_km is null, so POL-RD-05 has no amendment to re-quote and must not be given a substitute figure; and the vehicle type is RYDE_X, so POL-RD-12's pooled-itinerary baseline does not apply and the 3.2 km booked optimal stands untouched.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-02819", "EV-TRIP-02819"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04", "POL-RD-05", "POL-RD-12"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The fare model on this trip is METERED and the trip record carries no quoted_fare_sgd, so POL-RD-11's bar on distance-and-time refunds for upfront-quoted trips does not apply here, and POL-RD-02's arithmetic is the operative remedy rather than the pass-through correction alone. The surge multiplier is read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier, which records 1.0, as POL-RD-02 requires; the trip record does not carry that field at all and no higher multiplier may be assumed.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02819"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-11", "POL-RD-02"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "If the tribunal finds the deviation established, the POL-RD-02 computation is ((3.80 + 0.75 x 3.2 + 0.28 x 6.0) x 1.0) + 0.80 platform fee + 0.00 ERP + 0.00 waiting time - 0.00 promo = 8.68, against a charged total of 9.64; the refund is 0.96, which is above the SGD 0.50 de minimis and far below 90% of the charged total, so the outcome would be PARTIAL_REFUND, rounded up to SGD 1.00. The rider asks for that figure only if establishment is found on the trace.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02819"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.recomputed_fare",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's 60-day profile does not engage POL-RD-08's additional corroboration requirement. rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d is 1 and rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d_substantiated is 0, below the clause's trigger of 4 or more claims with 1 or fewer substantiated, so the excess the rider has shown is to be decided on this trip's trace evidence and no corroboration beyond the trace may be demanded of this claim.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-02819"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "I concede the point the record will not carry. On the governing trace figure the excess is 0.76 km, which is not greater than 0.8 km, and POL-RD-01 requires both the percentage and the absolute limb to pass; the rider therefore does not ask the tribunal to find the deviation established and does not ask it to read the threshold any other way. The two distance fields on this record straddle that threshold by 40 metres - 0.76 km on the trace, 0.80 km on the rounded copy - and the policy resolves the straddle against the rider by making the trace figure govern, so the shortfall is the rider's and the rider says so.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02819", "EV-TRIP-02819"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "NO_ACTION",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To both parties: the deviation gate fails and the fare already charged stands. The governing distance is the GPS trace, EV-GPS-02819, which measures 3.96 km; the booked optimal route on EV-TRIP-02819 is 3.2 km. The excess is therefore 0.76 km, or 23.75% of the optimal route. POL-RD-01 requires BOTH limbs to pass: the excess must be greater than 20% of the optimal distance AND greater than 0.8 km in absolute terms. The percentage limb passes (23.75% > 20%), but the absolute limb fails (0.76 km is not greater than 0.8 km). The trace figure governs and the trip record's rounded 4.0 km may not be used for the threshold test; even that figure gives exactly 0.80 km, which likewise is not greater than 0.80 km. No deviation is established, and POL-RD-01 directs the outcome NO_ACTION however the rider characterises the trip. The SGD 9.64 charged on EV-FARE-02819 stands and the SGD 1.50 the rider contests is not returned. This is not a win for either side on the merits of the route; it is the threshold doing its job.\n\nNo adjustment clause displaces the 3.2 km baseline. The trip record carries no amendment (pickup_amended_at, dropoff_amended_at and amended_optimal_distance_km are all null), so POL-RD-05 cannot run. The vehicle is RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL, so POL-RD-12's matched-itinerary baseline does not apply. The chat log EV-CHAT-02819 carries zero messages, so POL-RD-04's rider-instruction route is unavailable and its 200 m test cannot be run.\n\nThe driver's explanation 'One-way streets' is an external-traffic assertion with no traffic_advisory behind it. EV-ADVIS-02819-01 is MISSING, weight_multiplier 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT. Under POL-RD-13 and POL-RD-08 that assertion carries no weight and exonerates nothing. It does not need to: the excess never reaches the threshold, so nothing turns on it, and no escalation follows from the missing advisory because no party cited the absent identifier.\n\nNothing else is refundable. EV-FARE-02819 shows ERP of 0.00 with no gantries, no airport surcharge, no waiting-time fee and no promo discount, so there is no billing-integrity defect and no POL-RD-09(4) referral. The trace is not impaired for policy purposes (45 fixes at a 10-second interval, 100.0% coverage, zero gaps, max gap 0.0 s), so POL-RD-07 and POL-RD-10(3) are not engaged. All three deciding artifacts carry trip TRP-02819 with consistent timestamps, so POL-RD-10(2) and (4) are excluded. The driver profile, EV-DPROF-02819, shows 1 deviation flag in 90 days against 314 completed trips — far below the POL-RD-06 pattern test — so there is no conduct referral and no FULL_REFUND uplift. The rider's own POL-RD-02 arithmetic (recomputed fare 8.68 against a charged total of 9.64, a refund of 0.96 rounded up to SGD 1.00) is not reached, because that computation only runs once a deviation is established. Confidence is 0.90, capped by the weight-1.0 artifacts (EV-GPS-02819 and EV-TRIP-02819) that carry the deciding measurement. The monetary effect is nil, below the automatic execution threshold, so no amount moves."
  },
  "discarded_claims": [
    {
      "claim": "The absent advisory does not turn this into an escalation. Under POL-RD-13(1), where the asserting party names no evidence ID for an advisory, the missing advisory is not an exculpatory clause invoked against a cited artifact within POL-RD-10(5): an assertion that cites no artifact cannot be invoked against one, and the absence of an artifact no party has cited is a gap in the bundle rather than a contradiction in it. The driver's statement cites no advisory identifier, so POL-RD-10(5) does not fire on account of the traffic explanation.",
      "side": "DRIVER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-02819-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"
    }
  ]
}

