  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "NO_ACTION",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 1.0,
    "explanation": "To both parties: this case turns on a single arithmetic gate in POL-RD-01, and it fails by 40 metres.\n\nMEASUREMENT. The governing distance is the GPS trace, EV-GPS-02819, at trace_distance_km 3.96 km — not the rounded 4.00 km convenience copy on the trip record, because POL-RD-01 says the trace figure governs where the two disagree and the rounded copy may not be cited for the threshold test. The booked optimal route is 3.20 km (EV-TRIP-02819, optimal_distance_km). Excess = 3.96 − 3.20 = 0.76 km, which is 23.75% of optimal.\n\nTHE GATE. POL-RD-01 establishes a deviation only where the excess is BOTH greater than 20% of optimal AND greater than 0.8 km absolute. The percentage limb passes (23.75%). The absolute limb fails: 0.76 km is not greater than 0.80 km. Because both limbs must pass, no deviation exists on this trip and the outcome is NO_ACTION however the trip is characterised. The rider advocate's concession to precisely this effect is accepted, and the rider is right that the two distance fields straddle the threshold — the policy resolves that straddle against the rule the rider seeks. The driver advocate's threshold claims are accepted for the same reason: even on the rounded 4.00 km copy the excess is exactly 0.80 km, which still does not exceed 0.80 km, so the result is identical whichever field is read.\n\nCONSEQUENCES OF NO DEVIATION. POL-RD-02 does not run: there is no established deviation against which to recompute the fare, so the recomputed figure of 8.68 and the 0.96 difference against the charged total of 9.64 are not reached and are not paid. The contest is therefore not the rider's SGD 1.50 in the sense claimed. No exculpatory adjustment is needed on either side: POL-RD-04 supplies nothing because EV-CHAT-02819 carries zero messages and its 200 m corroboration test cannot be run; POL-RD-05 supplies nothing because pickup_amended_at, dropoff_amended_at and amended_optimal_distance_km are all null and no substitute re-quote may be invented; POL-RD-12 does not apply because the vehicle type is RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL. POL-RD-11 likewise does not apply: fare_model is METERED and no quoted_fare_sgd exists, so the upfront-pricing bar is irrelevant here. The 3.20 km comparator stands untouched.\n\nTRACE INTEGRITY. EV-GPS-02819 is not impaired for policy purposes: 100.0% coverage, 45 fixes at a 10-second interval against a 10-second expected interval, zero gaps and max_gap_sec 0.0 — none of POL-RD-07(a) to (c) is met. The POL-RD-10(3) escalation route is therefore not engaged and no independent corroboration is demanded.\n\nTHE DRIVER'S TRAFFIC EXPLANATION. The driver's account ('One-way streets') is moot rather than decisive: there is no established deviation for it to excuse, and it supplied no adjusted optimal. For completeness, the bundle holds no traffic advisory for this corridor — EV-ADVIS-02819-01 is MISSING with weight_multiplier 0.0 and issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT — so POL-RD-03 cannot be run on the record and, under POL-RD-13, an assertion of an external traffic cause that cites no advisory identifier is a gap in the bundle, not a POL-RD-10(5) escalation, and it neither reduces the excess nor supplies an amended optimal.\n\nOTHER ROUTES CHECKED AND CLOSED. POL-RD-09: EV-FARE-02819 shows erp_lines totalling 0.00 with no gantries, tolls_erp 0.0, airport_surcharge 0.0, waiting_time_fee 0.0 and surge_multiplier 1.0; there is no off-route or phantom gantry, no wrongly applied surcharge and no billing-integrity finding, so no POL-RD-09(4) referral. POL-RD-06: driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 1 (below 3) and 1/314 completed trips is about 0.3% (below 5%), so no repeat-deviation pattern is established, no FULL_REFUND uplift follows and no POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral issues. POL-RD-08: rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d is 1 with 1 substantiated (below the 4-or-more / 1-or-fewer trigger), so no extra corroboration is demanded — but the rider's initial burden still requires an excess meeting the POL-RD-01 threshold, and none exists. Only the profile fields that POL-GEN-01 names were used; every other profile field on either side is context only.\n\nESCALATION CHECKED. Trip identifiers match across EV-TRIP-02819, EV-GPS-02819 and EV-FARE-02819 (all TRP-02819); the trace's first and last fixes (16:25:31 and 16:32:51 on 2026-08-28) coincide with the trip record's start and completion and no timestamps run backwards; every charge line (base fare 3.80, distance charge for the billed distance, time charge for the billed duration, platform fee 0.80) has a counterpart in the trip record and trace; there is no chat detour request and no mutually contradictory evidence of comparable strength; and no refund anywhere approaches SGD 150.00 or the charged total. No POL-RD-10 trigger fires.\n\nOUTCOME. Under POL-GEN-03, NO_ACTION on a rider-filed dispute means the filing party's claim is not supported and the present state stands: EV-FARE-02819 records payment_status CHARGED, total_charged 9.64 and refund_issued_sgd 0.00, and those are left as they are. Nothing moves to either party. The monetary effect is SGD 0.00, below the POL-GEN-05 automatic-execution threshold of SGD 8.00. Confidence is 1.0 because every artifact carrying the deciding facts — the trace distance on EV-GPS-02819 and the optimal distance on EV-TRIP-02819 — carries weight_multiplier 1.0, and the missing advisory carries no fact at all."
  },
